  "schema_version": 1,
  "decision": "docs/adr/0559-duckdb-in-the-publisher-runs-every-transform-and-query-spark-keeps-only-table-maintenance-and-a-transform-moves-only-on-an-engine-equality-verdict.md",
  "purpose": "Single source of truth for the DuckDB extension files a release carries beside the publisher (root ADR-0559 §6). The publisher's bundled DuckDB reads Bronze objects and Iceberg tables on R2 through them, loaded by path from the release and never downloaded at run time: automatic install and load stay off (root ADR-0127). The release build fetches each pinned download through scripts/ci/fetch_pinned.py, unpacks it, holds the file to the digest and size below, puts it under `directory` in the release's files, and then runs that release's own publisher with no network (`verify-lakehouse-engine-extensions`) before anything is signed; release admission holds the installed files to this contract again. A build of an extension only loads into the DuckDB it was built for, so `duckdb_version` and `platform` are what the bundled DuckDB must report, and raising the `duckdb` crate means raising every pin here in the same pull request.",
  "duckdb_version": "v2.0.0",
